    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are hex and go on the wire unchanged: the read example asks for starting register 00h 20h (0020h-0023h). Parameter nXXX lives at its hex address in Table 4.4 (n003 = 0103h, n153 = 0199h); ENTER/ACCEPT are printed as 900/910."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus Communication Manual V7 and V74X Drives",
    "doc_number": "TM.V7.11 Rev 07-01",
    "revision_date": "2007-01-05",
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TM.V7.11&cmd=documents&documentName=TM.V7.11.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 19 (03h example), p. 41 (command registers), p. 42 (broadcast), pp. 43-44 (monitor registers), p. 45 (n003/n004), p. 52 (n151-n157), p. 56 (ENTER/ACCEPT)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "n153 defaults to 0, so a factory-fresh drive has no valid Modbus slave address; set n153 to 1-31 first. The defaults block shows the printed parameter defaults (n153 = 0, n154 = 2 = 9600, n155 = 2 = none).",
    "Left out because the sign is not stated: 002Fh frequency reference bias, 0032h torque monitor, 0037h output power, 0038h-003Ah PID feedback/input/output.",
    "Frequency registers follow n152 (default 0 = 0.1 Hz) and are left unscaled.",
    "The CM091/CM092 Modbus TCP/IP option card uses a different command layout (Table 4.5) that is not covered here.",
    "Broadcast (slave 0): 0001h bit 0 run, bit 1 reverse, bit 4 external fault, bit 5 fault reset; 0002h fixed at 30000 = 100 % of n011."
  ],
